// The repository's Markdown lint configuration, seeded once by
// spec-driven-docs. The project owns this file: edit it freely, and a later
// landing keeps its bytes.
//
// It loads the relative-links rule, which fails a relative link whose target
// does not exist. Every other rule takes the linter's default here, and the
// documentation root's own configuration merges over this one beneath it.
//
// Put a Markdown path the linter must skip in `ignores`. The `reserved:` list
// in .spec-driven-docs/config.yaml scopes sdd's own gates, not this linter.
// The linter skips the skill packages sdd lands, which keep the form sdd
// writes. A project's own skills beside them stay under the linter.
{
  "customRules": ["markdownlint-rule-relative-links"],
  "config": {
    "relative-links": true
  },
  "ignores": [
    ".claude/skills/sdd-setup/**",
    ".claude/skills/sdd-write-docs/**",
    ".agents/skills/sdd-setup/**",
    ".agents/skills/sdd-write-docs/**"
  ]
}
